> 
> Usage: cobc-rs [options] <source.cob>
> 
> Modes:
>   -x                    build a launch artifact (launcher + manifest; NOT a native executable)
>   -m                    build a loadable-module launch artifact (run via `cobcrun <name>`)
>   -fsyntax-only         parse + check only (no execution, no artifacts)
>   -E                    preprocess-only (define/copy expansion with #line headers)
>   -M [-MF file] [-MT t] make-style dependency output
> 
> Options:
>   -std=<name>           dialect (default|ibm|mf|mvs|cobol85|cobol2002|cobol2014|...)
>   -conf=<file.conf>     dialect configuration file
>   -free | -fixed | -fformat=<fmt>   source format
>   -I <dir>              copybook search path (repeatable)
>   -D<NAME>[=value]      conditional-compilation define
>   -o <path>             output artifact path
>   --compat=strict|gnucobol-testsuite   option policy
>   --print-capabilities  list supported/translated/ignored/rejected options
>   --explain-translation <opts...>     explain each option's policy
>   --dump-invocation-json <path>       write the structured invocation record
>   --version | --info | --dumpversion | --runtime-conf | --help
> 
> The candidate is an interpreter: it emits launch manifests, never native code.
> ,cobc-rs (gnucobol-rs, reproducing GnuCOBOL) ¿Ä‚␀
> A native-Rust COBOL front end + interpreter (ported runtime) with a cobc-shaped
> compatibility driver. NOT GnuCOBOL; no native code generation; no libcob linked.
> License LGPL-3.0-or-later. Not affiliated with the GNU project.
> ␀-W-xbuild-and-link mode: for the interpreter this means "prepare an executable launch artifact" (launcher + manifest); the artifact is NOT a native COBOL executable-mmodule mode: build a loadable-module launch artifact (manifest + launcher) resolvable by `cobcrun <name>` from the build-local module registry-ccompile to object: the candidate has no native object model (no C emission); reject honestly-Scompile to assembler: no native codegen; reject honestly-Cgenerate C: the candidate is an interpreter, not a C emitter; reject honestly-Epreprocess-only: emit the define/copy-expanded source (with the GnuCOBOL `#line` header shape)-fsyntax-onlyrun the real candidate check pipeline (preprocess, lex, parse, declarations/layout) and exit without executing or emitting artifacts-Mdependency mode: emit make-style dependency output (with -MF/-MT)-MFdependency output file-MTdependency target name (repeatable)-q--quietsuppress non-error messages: cobc-rs diagnostics are already minimal; no semantic effect-v--verboseverbose progress: informational only; the candidate records its own ledger-bembedded build (combine compile+link into one step in a specific way): not supported-j--jobjob name: the candidate has no shared-memory job model; accepted only for the -j / --job=name spelling with no effect-jddebug job: requires the shared-memory job model; reject honestlydebug job (graphical): requires the shared-memory job model; reject honestly-rrun module: cobc -r would exec the module; the candidate model rejects this form-Ffree-format source with module extensions: reject honestly-P-suppress COPY output during -E: not supported-Xrefcross-reference listing: no listing model; reject honestly-tlisting file: no listing model; reject honestly-t-listing to stdout: no listing model; reject honestly-T-listing to terminal: no listing model; reject honestly-tlineslisting line count: no listing model; reject honestly-tsymbolssymbol listing: no listing model; reject honestly-save-tempskeep inte